{
  "_comment": [
    "Copy to <data_dir>/config/sweep.json and edit. Read by deploy/run-conductor-scheduled.ps1.",
    "Order is priority: the sweep walks this list head-first and stops at the first candidate that",
    "actually ran rounds. A thread NOT listed here is never picked up at all — silently.",
    "",
    "Each candidate needs project / thread_id / repo_dir. repo_dir is the implementer's own CLONE",
    "for that project (not a linked worktree, and never the checkout the daemon itself is running",
    "from — the implementer would be editing its own running code).",
    "",
    "`requires` (OPTIONAL) is an array of exclusive-resource lease names the candidate needs BEFORE",
    "it may launch (T-exclusive-resource-lease-queue). If any named resource is already held by a",
    "different candidate, this one is enqueued FIFO and skipped this tick (disposition:",
    "lease-waiting) — it does not consume the tick's launch slot. When the holder finishes / is",
    "reclaimed for idle, the first waiter promotes automatically on the next sweep.",
    "",
    "v1 knows about the resource name `editor` (the interactive PIE / editor session on the",
    "wrapper host; two candidates cannot legitimately hold it at once). The mechanism is name-",
    "agnostic — future ticks may add `runner`, `bridge-55557`, `repo:mindwire-impl`, DDC, etc.",
    "There is no enum validation: a resource name is simply a coordination token, and an operator",
    "may reserve a name today that the mechanism only starts probing tomorrow.",
    "",
    "Do NOT list T-pr-review-* threads: they resolve to `NEXT: pr-review <ref>`, which fires the",
    "Tier B PR-gate against the paid Lexora/Gemini backend. Driving those from an unattended sweep",
    "would spend money on a timer, so it stays an explicit human action."
  ],
  "candidates": [
    {
      "project": "spirrow-voxelworld",
      "thread_id": "T-example-live-design-thread",
      "repo_dir": "C:/workspace/sandbox/voxelworld-impl",
      "requires": ["editor"]
    },
    {
      "project": "spirrow-mindwire",
      "thread_id": "T-example-mindwire-thread",
      "repo_dir": "C:/workspace/sandbox/mindwire-impl"
    }
  ]
}
